course: dictionary
lesson: 11854
title: Words about tails
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can name a thing, describe a thing, or be a nickname. «Bobtail» can be a noun, meaning a short tail or an animal with one. It can also be an adjective, as in «a bobtailed cat». Read the words around it to see which one it is.
explain: «The rabbit flicked its bobtail and hopped into the hedge.» Here the bobtail is the short tail itself, because the rabbit flicks it. «The bobtail cat curled up by the fire.» Here bobtail describes the cat: it is a cat with a short tail.
explain: Sometimes a word is a nickname. «The bobtail barked loudly at the postman.» The clues are a big, shaggy dog that barks. In everyday British talk, «bobtail» is a nickname for the Old English Sheepdog, so this is the dog's nickname, not its tail.
fact: A bobtail is a short tail, or a tail that has been cut short.
fact: A bobtail can also be an animal with a short tail, such as a bobtail cat or a rabbit.
fact: In everyday British talk, «bobtail» is a nickname for the Old English Sheepdog, a big shaggy dog.
fact: «Bobtailed» is an adjective that describes an animal with a short tail.
fact: The old phrase «ragtag and bobtail» meant a ragged crowd of people.
exercise: «The rabbit flicked its bobtail and vanished into the hedge.» What is the bobtail here? | A long ear | A hole in the ground | *A short tail | A thick bush
exercise: «The bobtail herded the sheep across the field.» Which dog is the bobtail in this sentence? | *The Old English Sheepdog, a big shaggy dog | A tiny mouse | A kind of rain | A type of boat
exercise: «The bobtailed cat curled up by the fire.» What does bobtailed describe? | *The cat, which has a short tail | The cat's owner | The fire, which is warm | The rug, which is soft
test: «The bobtail barked loudly at the postman.» In this sentence, what is a bobtail? | A letter carrier | *A big shaggy dog, the Old English Sheepdog | A loud bell | A bunch of flowers
test: In the old phrase «ragtag and bobtail», what did bobtail mean? | *A ragged crowd | A long, thin road | A type of bread | A kind of fish
exam: «The bobtail cat chased the mouse across the kitchen.» What does bobtail tell us about the cat? | *Its tail is short | Its tail is red | It is very hungry | It cannot run
